kosha count

  -- count: the numeric measure of a collection after all events.
  -- the bridge between everyday language and arithmetic.
  -- "4 apples" → count = 4
  -- "8 birds, 3 flew away, 2 came back" → count = 7
  --
  -- count IS sankhya of a vrnda (collection) — not a physics quantity.
  -- count-chain.tantra3 scans the event sequence and emits [count, sankhya, result].
  -- no separate count-total or count-remaining — the chain computes the right answer.
  -- the result word (total/remaining/left) is just a language alias for count.
  --
  -- the structure IS the reasoning:
  --   departure verbs (flew, ate, lost, gave) → subtract next operand
  --   arrival verbs (came, bought, found, got) → add next operand
  --   no verb → add (default: accumulation)

  "number-varga-vishesa"
  "math-varga-vishesa"
  "common-sense-varga-yukta"

  "sankhya-swarupa"
  "vrnda-yukta"
  "arithmetic-yukta"
  "vrnda-ganita-abheda"

  shabda word:count,number,many,how-many,quantity,total,remaining,left,sum,altogether,combined,rest,leftover / how-many-of-a-thing-after-all-events

done
